.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt OES 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oes
.Nd OpenEndpointSecurity event monitoring and authorization framework
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the driver as a module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
oes_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
framework provides endpoint-security event monitoring and authorization,
inspired by Apple's Endpoint Security API but built on the
.Fx
MAC framework and the Capsicum capability model.
It registers a MAC policy whose hooks turn kernel security-relevant operations
into events, and exposes them to userland clients through the
.Pa /dev/oes
character device.
The
.Xr liboes 3
library is the supported client interface.
.Pp
Events are of two kinds.
.Bl -tag -width "NOTIFY" -offset indent
.It AUTH
Authorization events are delivered from sleepable MAC check hooks; a subscribed
client may allow or deny the operation, and the operation blocks until the
client responds or the per-client timeout expires.
.It NOTIFY
Notification events are informational and never block the originating thread.
.El
.Pp
Multiple clients, in different processes, may be active at once.
Each
.Xr open 2
of
.Pa /dev/oes
creates an independent client with its own subscription set, muting state, mode,
and decision cache; events fan out to every subscribed client.
The maximum number of concurrent clients is bounded by the
.Va security.oes.max_clients
tunable.
.Pp
A client subscribes to event types with the
.Dv OES_IOC_SUBSCRIBE
ioctl, reads events with
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr poll 2 ,
.Xr select 2 ,
or
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
and answers authorization events with
.Dv OES_IOC_RESPOND .
Processes and paths may be muted per client so that their events are suppressed.
.Ss MAC hooks
Events are generated from MAC policy hooks, including process execution and
credential changes, the file lifecycle
.Pq open, close, create, unlink, rename, link, truncate ,
memory mapping, extended attributes and ACLs, mounts, module load and unload,
and socket and pipe operations.
File
.Em close
events are delivered via the
.Fn mac_vnode_check_close
hook; because a close cannot be denied, close is a NOTIFY-only event.
.Ss DTrace
The framework defines an
.Nm
SDT provider with probes for authorization outcomes
.Pq allow, deny, timeout ,
event enqueue and drop, and decision-cache hit and miss.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va security.oes.max_clients
Maximum number of concurrent clients.
.It Va security.oes.require_auth_clients
When non-zero, operations that would generate an AUTH event are denied if no
client is subscribed to authorize them.
.It Va security.oes.default_self_mute
When non-zero, a new client is automatically muted against its own process.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /dev/oes" -compact
.It Pa /dev/oes
client device
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr liboes 3 ,
.Xr mac 4 ,
.Xr dtrace 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
framework first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard .
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
A client that subscribes to AUTH events can block or deny the corresponding
system operations; with
.Va security.oes.require_auth_clients
set, the absence of a client can deny operations outright.
Access to
.Pa /dev/oes
should therefore be restricted to trusted, privileged programs.
